# Knowledge harness

This repo (`sam-dev-site/leif-in-the-wind`) is the source of truth. Chat memory is not.

Before project work, read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/MISSION.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md`, and `docs/STATUS.md`.

If you make a lasting decision, append `docs/DECISIONS.md` in the same session. Update `docs/STATUS.md` before you finish.

When the owner signs off (`perfect`, `everything is working`, `save and commit`, `all set`, `good`, `done`, `push`), sync GitHub `main` to this PC in that turn (commit, push, merge a playtest PR if needed). Do not ask. Do not report a hash git did not print. Do not say it is only on this machine. See `.cursor/rules/commit-signoff.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/dev-loop.mdc`.

Bugs that are not the current Play live in `docs/BUGS.md`. Log them there and leave them. When the owner asks to do bug fixes, read that file and name the open headings before changing the game. New wishes stay in `docs/IDEAS.md`.

Never invent biome species. If it is not in `docs/research/biomes/`, research it with sources first.

Prefer cloud agent + PR over loading this Surface Pro. Local machine is for playtest. Cloud never opens Godot. A local session names the next owner action (Play, Build in Cloud, or a new chat).

Slice docs do not override `docs/MISSION.md`. Features serve the named aesthetics (sensation, fantasy, discovery, submission), not only inland movement.

`docs/IDEAS.md` is an unordered set of slices. When the owner asks what to work on next, read the mission, decisions, status, and that file, and choose one slice. Do not treat the ideas file as a queue. Logging a wish adds questions grounded in the game and does not invent answers. See `.cursor/rules/ideas.mdc`.
